**Convention 2.2 (paid shallow and full prediction boundaries).** For
$D\ge2$, [PPF, Theorem 4.2][PPF] actually acquires

$$
e=\pi_{D-1}(v)\in S_{D-1}
\tag{CCF.5}
$$

with simultaneous optimal worst preparation projections

$$
(\mathsf{Reads},\mathsf{letters},\mathsf{peak})
=\bigl(2^{D-2},(D-1)2^{D-2},D-1\bigr)
\tag{CCF.6}
$$

when no name cap is imposed. It exports exactly $N_{D-1}$ names.
With exactly this acquired $e$, its original selected-target reader needs
at most one later Read. That service is reused unchanged.

For $D\ge1$, the same published acquisition routine
$\operatorname{Acquire}(R,D-1)$ acquires
$c=\pi_D(v)$ with sufficient bounds

$$
\mathsf{Reads}\le2^{D-1},\qquad
\mathsf{letters}\le D2^{D-1},\qquad
\mathsf{peak}\le D.
\tag{CCF.7}
$$

This is [PPF, Lemma 4.1][PPF] with its specified inputs, not a new
acquisition optimum. One may instead have acquired $c$ through completion
from $e$; that acquisition is charged once. [PPF, Theorem 5.1][PPF]
separately supplies paid acquisition of an exact-$M_1(D)$ code, and
[SCE, §§5–6][SCE] separately prices pooling from other exports. None of
these codes or acquisition costs is identified with the conditional
refinements considered here.

